0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1170555132/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-06-29T22:24:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1170555132","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60522369?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/allieculp","id":60522369,"login":"allieculp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTIyMzY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### What happened?\r\n\r\nThe attached Python program which mixes TF and IREE, when run, produces:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python q.py\r\n15\r\n2022-06-15 15:21:39.632455: W tensorflow/core/common_runtime/gpu/gpu_bfc_allocator.cc:42] Overriding orig_value setting because the TF_FORCE_GPU_ALLOW_GROWTH environment variable is set. Original config value was 0.\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/google/home/phawkins/p/jax/q.py\", line 35, in <module>\r\n    print(np.asarray(module[\"main\"](x, y)))\r\n  File \"/usr/local/google/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py3.10.4/lib/python3.10/site-packages/iree/runtime/function.py\", line 129, in __call__\r\n    self._invoke(arg_list, ret_list)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/google/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py3.10.4/lib/python3.10/site-packages/iree/runtime/function.py\", line 153, in _invoke\r\n    self._vm_context.invoke(self._vm_function, arg_list, ret_list)\r\nRuntimeError: Error invoking function: /main_checkout/iree/runtime/src/iree/hal/cuda/stream_command_buffer.c:369: INTERNAL; CUDA driver error 'CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE' (400): invalid resource handle; cuLaunchKernel; while invoking native function hal.ex.submit_and_wait; while calling import;\r\n[ 1]   native hal.ex.submit_and_wait:0 -\r\n[ 0] bytecode jit__lambda__2.main:470 <stdin>:3:3\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have a hypothesis as to what's going wrong, namely that in this program two libraries (IREE and TF) are both using the same thread to manipulate the CUDA context. TF changes the CUDA context and IREE does not gracefully handle that!\r\n\r\nTF has logic to save and restore the context:\r\nhttps://cs.opensource.google/tensorflow/tensorflow/+/master:tensorflow/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_driver.cc;drc=fdfdc02affbcd7e76a293f7f89871614ec8fa316;l=142\r\n\r\nhowever note that it does not try to restore the original caller's CUDA context on exit.\r\n\r\nIn the spirit of being liberal in what we accept, IREE should tolerate having other libraries change the CUDA context.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport iree.compiler\r\nimport iree.runtime\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nimport tensorflow as tf\r\n\r\nir = \"\"\"\r\nmodule @jit__lambda_.2 {\r\n  func.func public @main(%arg0: tensor<i32>, %arg1: tensor<i32>) -> tensor<i32> {\r\n    %0 = mhlo.add %arg0, %arg1 : tensor<i32>\r\n    return %0 : tensor<i32>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nconfig = iree.runtime.system_api.Config(\"cuda\")\r\nbin = iree.compiler.compile_str(ir, target_backends=[\"cuda\"], input_type=\"mhlo\")\r\nvm_module = iree.runtime.VmModule.from_flatbuffer(bin)\r\nmodule = iree.runtime.load_vm_module(vm_module, config)\r\n\r\nx = np.array(7, dtype=np.int32)\r\ny = np.array(8, dtype=np.int32)\r\n\r\nprint(np.asarray(module[\"main\"](x, y)))\r\n\r\n\r\ntf.add(1, 2)\r\n\r\n\r\nvm_module = iree.runtime.VmModule.from_flatbuffer(bin)\r\nmodule = iree.runtime.load_vm_module(vm_module, config)\r\n\r\nprint(np.asarray(module[\"main\"](x, y)))\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\r\n\r\nRuntime\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ pip show iree-compiler iree-runtime tensorflow\r\nName: iree-compiler\r\nVersion: 20220523.147\r\nSummary: IREE Compiler API\r\nHome-page:\r\nAuthor: IREE Authors\r\nAuthor-email: iree-discuss@googlegroups.com\r\nLicense: Apache-2.0\r\nLocation: /usr/local/google/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/3.10.4/envs/py3.10.4/lib/python3.10/site-packages\r\nRequires: numpy, PyYAML\r\nRequired-by:\r\n---\r\nName: iree-runtime\r\nVersion: 20220523.147\r\nSummary: IREE Python Runtime Components\r\nHome-page: https://github.com/google/iree\r\nAuthor: IREE Authors\r\nAuthor-email: iree-discuss@googlegroups.com\r\nLicense: Apache-2.0\r\nLocation: /usr/local/google/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/3.10.4/envs/py3.10.4/lib/python3.10/site-packages\r\nRequires: numpy, PyYAML\r\nRequired-by:\r\n---\r\nName: tensorflow\r\nVersion: 2.9.1\r\nSummary: TensorFlow is an open source machine learning framework for everyone.\r\nHome-page: https://www.tensorflow.org/\r\nAuthor: Google Inc.\r\nAuthor-email: packages@tensorflow.org\r\nLicense: Apache 2.0\r\nLocation: /usr/local/google/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/3.10.4/envs/py3.10.4/lib/python3.10/site-packages\r\nRequires: absl-py, astunparse, flatbuffers, gast, google-pasta, grpcio, h5py, keras, keras-preprocessing, libclang, numpy, opt-einsum, packaging, protobuf, setuptools, six, tensorboard, tensorflow-estimator, tensorflow-io-gcs-filesystem, termcolor, typing-extensions, wrapt\r\nRequired-by:\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_at":"2022-06-29T22:24:08Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https: